    "body": "## Summary\n\nAmends **ADR-036** to reflect what the Commit-1 diagnostic actually found. **Attribute selectors and floats are already fully implemented** — the spec's premise was a misreading cascade from ADR-035.\n\nScope reframed to **`clear` property + navbox hide**. Both ship; the second fixes the actual remaining visible defect.\n\n## The measurement\n\n### Attribute selectors: fully implemented, 10/10 forms matched\n\n`selectors.hpp` has `SimpleKind::Attribute` + full `AttributeMatch` enum (`Presence`, `Exact`, `Prefix`, `Suffix`, `Contains`, `Word`, `Hyphen`). `selectors.cpp` has full parser + matcher. **ADR-008 shipped this five ADRs ago.**\n\nTested 10 forms including the exact Wikipedia rule `figure[typeof~='mw:File/Thumb']`. **All 10 MATCHED.**\n\n### Floats: already work correctly\n\n```html\n<figure class=\"mw-default-size mw-halign-left\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\">\n<figure class=\"mw-default-size mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\">\n```\n\nFirst thumbnail's `<img>` at `x=346` = exactly content-x + CSS `margin-left:1.4em` of a left-floating figure. Second at right edge. **Thumbnails were floating correctly all along.**\n\nThe `float:none !important` override is `@media (max-width:640px)` — doesn't apply at 1774.\n\n### ADR-035's \"partial\" was a misreading\n\nThe visible overlap in ADR-035's PNG was the **navbox at x=324**, not the thumbnails. The misreading cascade: navbox visible → assumed thumbnail problem → assumed attribute-selector gap → measurement refuted.\n\n## The actual remaining defect\n\nEvery screenshot since ADR-029 shows nav-like content at `x=324` overlapping the intro. That's a `<table class=\"navbox\">` or `.sidebar` variant. ADR-031's `.sidebar{display:none !important}` isn't matching it — likely a different class token.\n\n## Reframed scope\n\n### 1. `clear` property support (~40-50 lines)\n\nGenuinely not implemented. Consequence: consecutive same-side floats overlap instead of stacking. Current HTML article has no consecutive same-side thumbnails, so no visible delta today — but defensively correct.\n\n### 2. Navbox hide (~15 lines)\n\nCommit 1's diagnostic identifies the exact element/class at x=324. Commit 2 adds the viewport_css hide rule. Same documented-workaround pattern as ADR-029/030/031. **Fixes the visible defect the arc has been carrying since ADR-029.**\n\n## What does NOT ship\n\n- Attribute selector work: already exists\n- Float correctness: already correct\n\n## Visible delta (revised)\n\n| Check | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Navbox at x=324 | visible | **hidden** |\n| Article intro | overlapped | **clean** |\n| Consecutive same-side floats | overlap | **stack** (defensive) |\n| Thumbnail floats | correct | unchanged |\n\nFirst ADR since ADR-030 whose PNG change is a **fix to an existing defect** rather than a new feature.\n\n## Fifth misdiagnosis in the arc\n\nThe correction record now has:\n1. ADR-028 — grid was correct, header was the bug\n2. ADR-031 — float \"overlap\" was intro text misread\n3. ADR-034 — SVG intrinsic was 1×1, not 220×35\n4. ADR-035 — \"partial\" finding was correct behavior\n5. **ADR-036 (this amendment)** — whole spec premise was a misreading cascade\n\nEach preserved in place with original spec above, correction below.\n\n## What ships\n\n1. **This PR**: amendment (docs only)\n2. **Impl PR**: navbox diagnostic + `clear` support + navbox hide + tests\n3. **Docs PR**: ADR-036 status → Implemented, Post-ADR-036 notes\n\nRefs ADR-035, ADR-036\n",
